<urn:usf:cli-field-specification:rule-allowed-values:1> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Optional allowedValue declarations form a bounded nonempty set of literal string values for text or IRI fields only. Values must satisfy the declared lexical bounds and IRI syntax where applicable. Refuse unsupported value kinds, empty or oversized sets and incompatible bounds. A singleton derives const; larger sets derive enum. The generic record reader checks the same set before projection, including subject-derived values. No declaration establishes operational proof." <urn:usf:graph:cli-schema-primitives> .
