<urn:usf:cli-field-specification:rule-operational-rule-required:1> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "A rule IRI is a required reference, not evidence of an implemented rule. Derive its selected graph closure, applicability, dependencies, explanation and owning admission/proof semantics; require a separately admitted allowlisted implementation for operational assessment. Missing rule resources or implementation return explicit gaps. This amendment does not supply domain proof/recovery rules." <urn:usf:graph:cli-schema-primitives> .
